{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":2,"query":"name=Friedman&limit=10&title=The Lexus and the Olive Tree","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"Lexus and the olive tree","subTitle":"understanding globalization"},"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Friedman, Thomas L.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"Picador","dateIssued":"2012","edition":"1st Picador ed.","issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xxii, 490 p. ; 21 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"In this vivid portrait of the new business world, Thomas L. Friedman shows how technology, capital, and information are transforming the global marketplace, leveling old geographic and geopolitical boundaries. With bold reporting and acute analysis, Friedman dramatizes the conflict between globalizing forces and local cultures, and he shows why a balance between progress and the preservation of ancient traditions will ensure a better future for all. The Lexus and the Olive Tree is an indispensable look at power and big change in the age of globalization."},"tableOfContents":"Foreword to the 2000 edition -- Opening scene : the world is ten years old -- Part One. Seeing the system. The new system -- Information arbitrage -- The Lexus and the olive tree -- ... And the walls came tumbling down -- Microchip Immune Deficiency -- The golden straitjacket -- The electronic herd -- Part Two. Plugging into the system. DOScapital 6.0 -- Globalution -- Shapers, adapters and other new ways of thinking about power -- Buy Taiwan, hold Italy, sell France -- The golden arches theory of conflict prevention -- Demolition man -- Winners take all -- Part Three. The backlash against the system. The backlash -- The groundswell -- Part Four. America and the system. Rational exuberance -- Revolution is U.S. -- If you want to speak to a human being, press 1 -- There is a way forward.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Thomas L. Friedman."},"Originally published: New York : Farrar, Straus and Giroux, c2000.","Includes index."],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"International economic relations"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Free trade"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Capitalism","Social aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Technological innovations","Economic aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Technological innovations","Social aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Intercultural communication"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Globalization"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"United States","topic":"Foreign economic relations"}],"classification":{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HF1359 .F74 2012"},"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Lexus and the olive tree"},"name":{"namePart":"Friedman, Thomas L."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York : Picador, 2012","edition":"1st Picador ed."},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)1202769973"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990133982190203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781250013743"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1250013747"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"773667516"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/age